-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/4d583c0d-f643-5b2c-97d1-321a22db0951
-- title:
--   Base change for GL₂: elliptic–central class sums compared
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ a finite Galois extension, $\sigma : L \simeq_K L$ is an automorphism with $\sigma \ne 1$, and the hypotheses are as follows.
--
--   *Field-theoretic data.* The hypothesis `hprime` says that $[L:K] = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ is a prime number, and `hgen` says that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (written `σ.symm`), so that $\sigma^{-1}$ generates the Galois group. The real numbers $\alpha, \beta$ satisfy $0 < \alpha$ (`hα`) and $\alpha < \beta$ (`hαβ`). The finite set $S_K$ of finite places of $K$ (a `Finset` of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$) satisfies `hS`: every finite place $w$ of $L$ whose restriction `HeightOneSpectrum.under` to $K$ lies outside $S_K$ has ramification index $1$ over that restriction. The datum $D$ is an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28), that is, a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which is compatible with $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ acting on $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$ and continuous in each element; [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14) denotes the entrywise action of $D(\sigma^{-1})$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$.
--
--   *Measures on the idele class groups.* Haar measures $\nu_{Z,L}$ on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ and $\nu_{Z,K}$ on $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ are fixed, each group carrying its Borel structure. On $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ the measure used is `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 F) F` for the Borel structure `glBorel`.
--
--   *Characters.* $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top \le \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ such that the induced function $z \mapsto \xi_L(z)$ is continuous (`hξc`) and trivial on the image of $L^\times$ in $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ (`hξt`). $\Xi$ is a finite set of homomorphisms $\top \le \mathbb{A}_K^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$ characterised by `hΞ`: a character $\xi$ lies in $\Xi$ exactly when it is continuous, trivial on the image of $K^\times$, and satisfies $\xi \circ N = \xi_L$, where $N$ is the idelic norm `idelicNorm` of the base-change datum [`M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineDescent.html#L87) (the units map of the algebra norm $\mathbb{A}_L \to \mathbb{A}_K$).
--
--   *Representatives and fundamental domains on the $L$ side.* $R_L$ is a set of elements of $GL_2(L)$. By `hRLsub` it is contained in the set of those $\delta$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-norm class [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766) of the $\sigma^{-1}$-conjugacy class of $\delta$ equals the $GL_2(K)$-conjugacy class of some $\gamma$ lying in `ellipticCell K` (the characteristic polynomial of $\gamma$ has no root in $K$) or in `centralCell K` ($\gamma$ is a scalar matrix). By `hRL`, for every $\delta$ in that same set there is a unique $\delta_0 \in R_L$ with $\delta = u \cdot (h^{-1} \delta_0\, \sigma^{-1}(h))$ for some $h \in GL_2(L)$ and $u \in L^\times$ entering as the scalar matrix $u I_2$, where $\sigma^{-1}$ acts entrywise. For each $\delta_0 \in R_L$, $\Psi_L(\delta_0) \subseteq GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ is contained in the band $\{g : \lVert \det g \rVert \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΨLs`), where $\lVert \cdot \rVert$ is [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19), the distributive Haar character of the adele ring; and by `hΨL` it is a fundamental domain, for the restriction of `adelicGLHaar` to that band, for the image in $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ under `globalPoints` of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser `sigmaCentralizer`, namely $\{t \in GL_2(L) : t \delta_0 \sigma^{-1}(t)^{-1} = \delta_0\}$. Finally $\Theta \subseteq \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ is, by `hΘ`, a fundamental domain with respect to $\nu_{Z,L}$ for the range of the homomorphism $L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_L^\times$, $w \mapsto \sigma^{-1}(w)w^{-1}$.
--
--   *Representatives and fundamental domains on the $K$ side.* $R_K \subseteq GL_2(K)$ is contained in `centralCell K ∪ ellipticCell K` (`hRKsub`), and by `hRK` every $\gamma$ in that union has a unique $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ with $\gamma = a \cdot (h^{-1}\gamma_0 h)$ for some $h \in GL_2(K)$ and $a \in K^\times$ acting as the scalar matrix. For $\gamma_0 \in R_K$, $\Psi_K(\gamma_0) \subseteq GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ lies in the band $\{g : \lVert \det g\rVert \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΨKs`) and is, by `hΨK`, a fundamental domain for the image under `globalPoints` of the centraliser of $\gamma_0$ in $GL_2(K)$, with respect to the restriction of `adelicGLHaar` to that band.
--
--   *Local–global norm principle.* The hypothesis `hLG` states: for every $\gamma \in$ `ellipticCell K`, if for every finite place $v$ of $K$ there is $\delta_v \in GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ with `IsNormOf K L (v.adicCompletion K) σ.symm` for the image of $\gamma$ in $GL_2(K_v)$ — that is, the image of $\gamma$ in $GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ is conjugate to the $\sigma^{-1}$-norm string $\delta_v\,\sigma^{-1}(\delta_v)\cdots$ of length $[L:K]$ — and likewise over the infinite adele ring of $K$, then the conjugacy class of $\gamma$ is a norm class, [`LT.TwistedNorm.IsNormClass hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L785), i.e. lies in the range of `normClassMap hgen`.
--
--   *Matching of test functions.* The hypothesis `hEuler` states: for every Haar measure $\mu_L$ on $GL_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ (with the Borel structure `glBorelOf`) there exists $c_0 \in \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$, $c_0 \ne 0$, such that for every finite set $S'$ of finite places of $K$ with $S_K \subseteq S'$ and all $\varphi : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$, $f : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfying `AreMatchingAt K L σ.symm S' φ f` (the existence of archimedean, finite and semi-local/local components factorising $\varphi$ and $f$ in the sense of `IsSemiLocalFactorization` and `IsUnitFactorization`, together with archimedean matching and matching `AreMatchingLocal` at each $v \in S'$) and satisfying the unramified condition that for each $v \notin S'$ all of whose places of $L$ above it are unramified the indicators of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` and `localIntegralSet K v` are matching local functions, one has `AreMatchingOn K L (AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K) σ.symm μL (c₀ • adelicGLHaar)` for the pair consisting of $\varphi$ transported along the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ (`Algebra.TensorProduct.comm` followed by [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57)) and $f$; here `AreMatchingOn` asserts that coupled twisted orbital integrals of $\varphi$ and orbital integrals of $f$ agree whenever $\gamma$ is regular semisimple and a norm of a $\delta$ with regular semisimple norm string, and that the orbital integral of $f$ vanishes at a regular semisimple $\gamma$ which is not a norm.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Under these hypotheses there exists $c \in \mathbb{C}$ with $c \ne 0$ such that for every finite set $S'$ of finite places of $K$ with $S_K \subseteq S'$, and for all $\varphi : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ continuous and of compact support, $f : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathbb{C}$ continuous and of compact support, which satisfy `AreMatchingAt K L σ.symm S' φ f` and the unramified local matching condition at the places outside $S'$ all of whose places of $L$ above them are unramified, the following identity holds:
--   $$\sum_{\delta_0 \in R_L} e_L(\delta_0)^{-1} \int_{\Theta} \xi_L(z) \left( \int_{\Psi_L(\delta_0)} \varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\, \delta_0\, D(\sigma^{-1})(z\,x)\bigr)\, d\,\mathrm{adelicGLHaar} \right) d\nu_{Z,L} = c \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \sum_{\gamma_0 \in R_K} e_K(\gamma_0)^{-1} \int_{\mathbb{A}_K^\times} \xi_K(z) \left( \int_{\Psi_K(\gamma_0)} f\bigl(x^{-1}\,\gamma_0\, z\, x\bigr)\, d\,\mathrm{adelicGLHaar}\right) d\nu_{Z,K}.$$
--   Here both sums over $R_L$ and $R_K$ are `finsum`s over the respective sets and the sum over $\Xi$ is a finite sum; $\delta_0$ and $\gamma_0$ occur through their images under `globalPoints`, $z$ through the scalar matrix `centralScalar` $z$, and the $L$-side integrand applies the entrywise action `sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm` to the product of that scalar matrix with $x$. The constants are
--   $$e_L(\delta_0) = \#\bigl\{\, q \in L^\times/\{\sigma^{-1}(w)w^{-1} : w \in L^\times\} \ :\ q = [u] \text{ for some } u \in L^\times \text{ with } u\delta_0 = h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(h) \text{ for some } h \in GL_2(L) \,\bigr\},$$
--   $$e_K(\gamma_0) = \#\bigl\{\, a \in K^\times \ :\ a\gamma_0 = h^{-1}\gamma_0 h \text{ for some } h \in GL_2(K)\,\bigr\},$$
--   cardinalities taken as `Nat.card` and inverted in $\mathbb{C}$; the scalars $u$ and $a$ again act as scalar matrices. Note the asymmetry of the two sides: on the $L$ side the outer integral is over the fundamental domain $\Theta$, on the $K$ side over all of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$.
--
--   This is the comparison of the elliptic and central terms of the geometric side of the trace formula for $GL_2$ over $K$ with the $\sigma$-elliptic and central-norm terms of the twisted trace formula over $L$, in the cyclic prime-degree base-change situation of Langlands's Base Change for GL(2), stated after both sides have been unfolded along the (twisted) centralisers, so that only the class sums over $R_L$ and $R_K$ with their fundamental domains remain. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_twistedEllipticCentralFold_eq_mul_sum_kernelCentralEllipticFold_of_areMatchingOn_of_isNormClass`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_twistedEllipticCentralFold_eq_mul_sum_kernelCentralEllipticFold_of_areMatchingOn_of_isNormClass), where the two sides are recognised as the corresponding parts of the kernel expansions.
